# agent.skills — Phase-by-Phase Builder Agent (Single-user Prototype)

This agent builds the project incrementally from phase docs.
It can implement UI, tools, and integration layers while preserving architecture invariants.

## Primary Mission
Build a Generative UI Dashboard workbench:
- Left Canvas renders pinned widgets + persistent interactables.
- Right Dock hosts chat, uploads, DB tools, MCP config & approvals.
Generative UI is powered by Tambo component registration + tool calls. [1](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tambo-ai/react)[2](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/client/sampling)

## Constraints
- Single user only.
- SQLite upload is session-only, in-memory.
- MCP is client-side (browser -> MCP server). [7](https://modelcontextprotocol.info/docs/)[8](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol)
- Bun runtime is used to run Next (`bun --bun next ...`). [3](https://reactflow.dev/)[4](https://deepwiki.com/Skyvern-AI/skyvern/7.1-workflow-editor-architecture)

## Agent Workflow (for every phase)
1) Read `docs/phases/phase-N.md`.
2) Extract:
   - Objective
   - Additions (UI/components/tools)
   - State model changes
   - Acceptance checklist
3) Implement the smallest set of code changes to satisfy acceptance.
4) Ensure:
   - TypeScript passes
   - App runs with Bun
   - New actions emit Event Ledger records
5) Update any phase docs only if necessary.

## Capabilities (Skills)

### 1) RepoBootstrapSkill (Phase 0)
- Setup Bun scripts for Next (`bun --bun next dev/build/start`). [3](https://reactflow.dev/)[4](https://deepwiki.com/Skyvern-AI/skyvern/7.1-workflow-editor-architecture)
- Setup Tailwind + shadcn/radix baseline.
- Setup TamboProvider wiring. [1](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tambo-ai/react)[2](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/client/sampling)

### 2) WorkbenchSkill (Phases 1–3)
- Build split-pane workbench layout (Canvas/Dock).
- Implement Dock tabs.
- Implement event timeline view.

### 3) TamboComponentSkill (Phases 4–6)
- Define Tambo components with Zod props schemas and descriptive metadata. [1](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@tambo-ai/react)[2](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2025-06-18/client/sampling)
- Add one interactable component (TaskBoard).
- Add local tools callable by the agent (schema-defined).

### 4) PersistenceSkill (Phase 7+)
- Add localStorage persistence with schemaVersion.
- Persist thread state/events/widgets/templates without storing large payloads.

### 5) ArtifactIngestionSkill (Phases 12–20)
- Implement artifact types and derivation links.
- Integrate OSS parsers:
  - PDF.js text extraction. [9](https://www.w3resource.com/sqlite/snippets/sqlite-bun.php)[10](https://blog.openreplay.com/quick-guide-bun-sqlite-setup/)
  - tesseract.js OCR. [11](https://nextjs.org/conf/session/nextjs-bun)[12](https://bun.com/docs/guides/ecosystem/nextjs)
  - SheetJS xlsx parsing. [13](https://www.timsanteford.com/posts/how-to-ocr-with-tesseract-js-to-unlock-text-from-images/)[14](https://www.xjavascript.com/blog/how-to-extract-text-from-a-pdf-in-javascript/)
  - mammoth.js docx extraction. [15](https://tesseract.projectnaptha.com/)[16](https://blog.rasc.ch/2019/07/ocr-with-tesseractjs.html)
- Create derived artifacts (Text/Dataset) and auto-insight widgets.

### 6) MCPIntegrationSkill (Phases 21–23)
- Add client-side MCP server config UI stored in localStorage. [7](https://modelcontextprotocol.info/docs/)
- Wire MCP servers into TamboProvider.
- Add approval UX and provenance recording.
- Follow MCP Streamable HTTP transport considerations. [8](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol)

### 7) DatabaseSkill (Phases 24–29)
- SQLite in-memory via sql.js from uploaded file bytes. [5](https://github.com/sqlitebrowser/sqlitebrowser)[6](https://turso.tech/blog/5-best-free-sqlite-gui)
- Build schema extraction -> SchemaArtifact.
- Build query runner -> QueryResultArtifact.
- Visualization suggestions -> Graph component.
- ERD module using React Flow. [17](https://sql.js.org/)[18](https://sqlite.org/wasm/doc/trunk/demo-123.md)

### 8) ExplainabilitySkill (Phase 30)
- Build “Explain this dashboard” overlay using Event Ledger.
- Provide provenance graph widgetId -> artifacts -> tool calls -> MCP servers.

## Invariants (Never Break These)
- Canvas rendering is driven by WidgetInstances, not chat thread messages.
- Every artifact/tool/widget is identifiable via stable IDs.
- Every significant action emits an EventRecord.
- The agent must only call registered tools/components.
- UI remains usable without MCP/DB configured (graceful empty states).

## Output Expectations (when implementing a phase)
- Provide a concise plan.
- Implement the phase.
- Provide commands:
  - bun install
  - bun --bun next dev
- Provide test prompts or manual steps matching acceptance checklist.
